          "quote": "Then the chamber was heated up to a temperature of 400 °C. For both bi- and multilayered films, a soft Ti layer was firstly deposited on the substrate followed by a hard TiN layer. In this way, a multilayer with alternating soft Ti layer and hard TiN layer was produced. The multilayered film has a 100 nm repeat thickness, a 9:1 (TiN to Ti) constituent ratio, and contains 10 interfaces (Fig. 3). For the bilayered film, the thickness of the Ti and TiN layer is approximately 100 nm and 900 nm, respectively.",
